rgizer Holdings, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, manufactures, markets, and distributes household batteries, specialty batteries, and lighting products worldwide. It offers household batteries, including primary, rechargeable, specialty, and hearing aid under the Energizer, Eveready, Rayovac, and Varta brands; and protectants, wipes, tire and wheel care products, glass cleaners, leather care products, air fresheners, and washes under the Armor All, Nu Finish, Refresh Your Car!, LEXOL, Eagle One, NEVR-DULL, California Scents, Driven, Bahama & Co, Carnu, Grand Prix, Kit, Tempo, and Centralsul brands. The company also provides fuel and oil additives, functional fluids, and other performance chemical products under the STP brand; automotive air conditioning recharge products, other refrigerant and recharge kits, sealants, and accessories under the A/C PRO brand name. In addition, it distributes and markets lighting products comprising handheld, headlights, lanterns, and area lights; flashlights under the Hard Case, Dolphin, and WeatherReady brands; and licenses brands to developing consumer solutions in solar, automotive batteries, portable power for critical devices, generators, power tools, household light bulbs, and other lighting products. The company sells its products through direct sales force, distributors, and wholesalers, as well as retail locations, mass merchandisers and warehouse clubs, food, drug and convenience stores, electronics specialty stores and department stores, hardware and automotive centers, e-commerce, and military stores. Energizer Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 2015 and is headquartered in Saint Louis, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark S. LaVigne J.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $530K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $41K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Energizer Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $2.0B market cap on $2.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 40%.","The business throws off $228M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.49\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8272884283246972},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 58% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 21% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Insiders are net buyers (90% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $4.1M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","10 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Encounter (ASX:ENR) Extends Higher-Grade Niobium at Aileron","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/rare-earth-minerals/encounter-asxenr-extends-higher-grade-niobium-at-aileron","date":"2026-11-23","timestamp":1795411380.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"This Insider Has Just Sold Shares In Energizer Holdings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/household/nyse-enr/energizer-holdings/news/this-insider-